# M8b soundness — grants have DYNAMIC extent, not lexical scope.
# None of these `rq`s are lexically inside a `gr`, yet all succeed at runtime, so
# the checker must stay silent (authority is unknown inside escaped blocks, and `s
# is free somewhere, so it is grantable).
[ `s rq $sent$ . ] :send     # bound block: invoked later under a grant
`s [ send @ ] gr
[ `s rq ] `s \ gr            # block reaches `gr` through the stack (swap)
`s :k  k [ `s rq ] gr        # the granted capability arrived through a name
